# NetworkPolicy Troubleshooting with Cilium Hubble

Troubleshoot NetworkPolicy packet drops and traffic flow denials using the Cilium `hubble` CLI.

## 1. Prerequisites & Health Verification

Ensure Cilium and Hubble relay are active on the control plane node:

```bash
# Verify Cilium status
cilium status --wait

# Start Hubble port-forward if not already listening locally
cilium hubble port-forward &

# Verify local Hubble connectivity
hubble status
```

---

## 2. Tracing NetworkPolicy Drops in Real-Time

When Kubernetes NetworkPolicies block traffic, packets are dropped silently at the eBPF layer. Use Hubble's
`--verdict DROPPED` flag to capture these events live:

```bash
# Watch all dropped packets live in the backend namespace
hubble observe --namespace {{ cka_lab_networking_backend_namespace | default('cka-lab-net-backend') }} --verdict DROPPED -f

# Filter drops originating specifically from the client namespace
hubble observe --from-namespace {{ cka_lab_networking_client_namespace | default('cka-lab-net-client') }} --verdict DROPPED -f

# Filter drops targeting port 80
hubble observe --to-port 80 --verdict DROPPED -f
```

### Common Drop Verdicts

- `Policy denied (INGRESS)`: Inbound request was rejected by a default-deny rule or missing `ingress` allow rule.
- `Policy denied (EGRESS)`: Outbound request was blocked because destination namespace/pod or port is not permitted.

---

## 3. Verifying Allowed Connections

Confirm that authorized traffic flows successfully across namespaces:

```bash
# Observe allowed traffic from authorized client
hubble observe --from-pod {{ cka_lab_networking_client_namespace | default('cka-lab-net-client') }}/cka-lab-client-authorized -f

# Output in compact one-line format
hubble observe --namespace {{ cka_lab_networking_backend_namespace | default('cka-lab-net-backend') }} -o compact
```
